What the translation covers:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- Exported symbols match the C shared library exactly: [38;5;10mdriver[0m, [38;5;10mgood[0m, [38;5;10mbad[0m, [38;5;10mprintLine[0m, [38;5;10mprintIntLine[0m. The header has no namespace-renaming macros, so source names are the final linker symbols. [38;5;10mgoodG2B[0m/[38;5;10mgoodB2G[0m were [38;5;10mstatic[0m in C, so they stay private Rust functions.[0m[0m
- Output goes through the C [38;5;10mprintf[0m with the original [38;5;10m"%s\n"[0m / [38;5;10m"%d\n"[0m format strings rather than Rust's [38;5;10mprintln![0m, so stdout buffering and interleaving with a C caller's own output are preserved.[0m[0m
